    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_da56877d",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: overall-intent-description; overall-intent-description: The scene depicts a man in a kitchen, leaning over an open dishwasher, with text overlay reading 'i think i almost got my dishwasher working.' The visual element of steam rising from the dishwasher and the man's intense, focused expression are juxtaposed with the text to create a humorous, self-deprecating tone. The meme's intent is to convey the absurdity or difficulty of fixing a household appliance, using the man's exaggerated effort as a comedic device. There is no toxicity present in this meme; it does not target any protected group or contain hateful, abusive, cyberbullying, harmful, misogynous, or propagandistic content. The humor is derived from relatable domestic frustration, not from disparaging any group or individual.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_22b8295a"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
